# =============================================================================
# Build context for the root Dockerfile.
#
# Two jobs: keep the context small (a 305 MB logs/ folder was being uploaded to the daemon on every
# build), and keep anything credential-shaped out of it. The image restores through a BuildKit
# secret, so no NuGet credential file has any business in the context either.
# =============================================================================

# Build output
**/bin
**/obj
**/.smokeout
.smokeout/

# Logs (REQ-NFR-029 — these are large and regenerate on every run)
**/logs
logs/

# Test and agent artefacts
tests/.artifacts/
test-results/
test-results-*/
playwright-report/
.verify/
**/TestResults
uiIssues/

# Source control and IDE
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.*proj.user

# The MAUI head. net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0, not referenced by the web host, and nothing in a Linux
# image can build it — keeping it out of the context makes that explicit rather than incidental.
source/BlogApp/

# NOTE: .editorconfig is deliberately NOT ignored. It carries the analyzer severities, so excluding
# it would let the in-image build disagree with the local one about what is an error.

# Tooling and framework scaffolding that the image never needs
**/node_modules
.tfcore/
.claude/
.opencode/
.playwright-mcp/
.trblazeui/
scripts/
mockups/
docs/
deploy/
.github/

# Credentials and secrets — never in a build context (REQ-NFR-025)
**/.env
**/secrets.json
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
nuget.config
NuGet.Config

# Docker's own files and anything else with no role inside the image
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
**/docker-compose*
**/charts
**/azds.yaml
**/npm-debug.log
LICENSE.txt
*.md
*.html
package.json
package-lock.json
playwright.config.ts
